{"name":"Fisher King","hex":"#5182b9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Fisher King","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A figure of Arthurian legend, the last in a long line of British kings tasked with guarding the Holy Grail, but rendered impotent by a wound; he is sometimes depicted as spending his time fishing while he awaits a \"chosen one\" who can heal him."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Fisher_King"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fisher King","blocks":[{"text":"The Fisher King is a figure in the Arthurian legend, the last in a long line of British kings tasked with guarding the Holy Grail. The Fisher King is both the protector and physical embodiment of his lands, but a wound renders him impotent and his kingdom barren. Unable to walk or ride a horse, he is sometimes depicted as spending his time fishing while he awaits a hero who can heal him."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Perceval-arrives-at-grail-castle-bnf-fr-12577-f18v-1330-detail.jpg/330px-Perceval-arrives-at-grail-castle-bnf-fr-12577-f18v-1330-detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fisher_King"},{"title":"King","blocks":[{"text":"King is a royal title given to a male monarch. A king is an absolute monarch if he holds unrestricted governmental power or exercises full sovereignty over a nation. In a modern context, the title may refer to the ruler of one of a number of modern monarchies. The title of king is used alongside other titles for monarchs: in the West, emperor, grand prince, prince, archduke, duke or grand duke, and in the Islamic world, malik, sultan, emir or hakim, among others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg/330px-Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King"}],"ima